#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152187 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151989 :question/id #uuid "e57f9dab-c5db-55d9-9b21-375bbc92281c" :question/math-academy-id "e-6814" :question/problem "Consider the ellipse centered at the origin with horizontal radius $3$ and vertical radius $1,$ as shown below. Which set of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(3,0)?$ \n\n![](images/5d/5d791b30556f41973c8f1a9b8702744afae72458d0ce285de2b7ef8fa19d720a.png)" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx= a\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=b\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(a,0).$\n\nIn our case, $a=3$ and $b=1.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are\n\n$$\nx= 3\\cos\\theta,\\quad y=\\sin\\theta, \\quad \\theta \\in [0,2\\pi).\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db20f4a5-27a4-5fbc-aae2-2febf8f99cb1" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048432 :topic/math-academy-id 853 :topic/title "Introduction to Ellipses"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050722 :topic/math-academy-id 806 :topic/title "Parametric Equations of Circles"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152431 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db2b1ea6-2fc9-53f7-a4a4-a5e8cbc6a497" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 25\\cos θ, y = 9\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149118} {:answer/id #uuid "efb583fe-9343-5d88-b1b2-fbf7a81311b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x = 3\\cos θ, y = 5\\sin θ" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186149119} {:answer/id #uuid "01f3f2be-5819-5f75-be77-4d68b2cd0c04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/va