, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a semi-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](images/6d/6db43ff41344f292c8cb5805febd175088fe068fe89927bade0c6fc2246c8781.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[0,\\pi ]$, we get the semi-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the semi-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ].\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "275cbc97-498b-541f-b490-b72a4ab58e76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,2\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238396} {:answer/id #uuid "74ffffaa-f33b-547e-93c3-da339f101aac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239065} {:answer/id #uuid "97d904bb-b2da-58f1-80e3-6c632732919d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239372} {:answer/id #uuid "9a7be160-4c62-5f6d-9a5c-7c8834e48bb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [\\frac{3\\pi }{2},2\\pi ]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239399} {:answer/id #uuid "b456abd5-51b5-5847-b511-91f87dd5e414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b456abd5-51b5-5847-b511-91f87dd5e414" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239631} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f2a1dfb-0aab-5eed-a08a-01fe0d294c69" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-fie